## Implementation Details

### Configuration in main.jsx
```jsx
import { StrictMode } from 'react'
import { createRoot } from 'react-dom/client'
import './index.css'
import App from './App.jsx'
import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react"

createRoot(document.getElementById('root')).render(
  <StrictMode>
    <App />
    <Analytics />
  </StrictMode>,
)
```

This follows the official Vercel Analytics React/Vite quickstart guide fetched from:
https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

## Next Steps for Deployment

To enable analytics data collection:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the project's Analytics tab in the Vercel dashboard
3. Click "Enable Web Analytics" if not already enabled
4. Analytics will start collecting data after the next deployment

## Browser Verification

Once deployed, you can verify the integration by:
1. Opening browser DevTools (Network tab)
2. Visiting the deployed application
3. Looking for requests to `/_vercel/insights/view` or similar analytics endpoints
4. Checking the Vercel dashboard for incoming analytics data

## Notes
- The project uses React 19.2.6 and Vite 8.0.16
- Analytics component is compatible with React's StrictMode
- No additional configuration required in vite.config.js
- Analytics will track page views automatically
- Development mode includes analytics for testing purposes
